  "body": "Stacked on #1772 (branched from its head 0cbd404d). The base is `main` because `issue/1749-pocket3d-open-notch` exists only on the fork; until #1772 merges, this PR's diff also shows #1772's commits. Only commit 752d6c13 is new. Merge #1772 first, then `git merge origin/main` here.\n\n## What changed\n- **Stock far past the silhouette gets cleared** (case 2). `machining3d::open_sides` now takes the setup's stock outline. The #1749 band grows from (silhouette ∪ stock outline) by r − 0.01 mm, less the other parts. A whole-model 3D Pocket and Multi-Axis Rough now clear the stock around the model out to the stock's edge, down to Bottom Z, the way the 2D pocket has since #12. If no stock is set up, the result is the same as with #1749.\n- **Tilted case (case 1) cannot be built.** `OpParams::tilt()` returns `None` for `Pocket3D` and `MultiAxisRough`, so no frame ever reaches their arms. The `tilted` branch of `operation::open_side::open_footprint` used to keep the old footprint without saying so. It now refuses by name (`TILTED_OPEN_SIDE`), so a tilt added to these kinds later cannot quietly leave a ridge.\n- Decision: `docs/decisions/1774-pocket3d-open-far-tilted.md`.\n- **Output change:** any whole-model 3D Pocket or Multi-Axis Rough whose stock reaches more than about 2 tool radii past the model now cuts that stock too. Picked and Boundary-controlled regions are unchanged.\n\n## Pinning tests\n- `pocket3d_open_side::stock_far_past_the_silhouette_is_cleared_to_the_stock_outline`: a 70 mm stock around a 30 mm notched part. The stock left at the stock edge and on a ring at 28 mm must be at the floor. Also checks no gouge (no cutter disc inside the part) and that verify is clean.\n- `operations::multiaxis_rough_clears_the_far_stock_the_pocket_clears`: Multi-Axis Rough and the 3D Pocket run the same ladder on a 70 mm stock. Both reach the far stock, and the far stock adds cuts compared with a 40 mm stock.\n- `operation::open_side::law::a_tilted_whole_model_refuses_by_name` (lib unit test) and `pocket3d_open_side::no_3d_pocket_kind_carries_a_tilt` (pins the premise).\n- Changed: `level_links::a_helix_under_the_bore_floor_is_never_silent`. Its \"nothing below Z 0 anywhere\" assert now reads \"every move below Z 0 keeps its 5 mm disc off every projected part facet\". The stock around the part is now cut down to the stock bottom it asks for. The no-move-under-the-bore and verify-clean asserts are kept.\n\n## Mutation checks (each: mutate, confirm red, restore, touch, cmp against a backup)\n- Stock union in `open_sides` disabled: `stock_far_...` red (\"keeps Z 32.000 at (34.90, -34.90)\").\n- Tilted refusal deleted: `a_tilted_whole_model_refuses_by_name` red.\n- Pocket3D arm passing `None` for the stock: `stock_far_...` red.\n- Multi-Axis Rough arm passing `None`: `multiaxis_rough_clears_the_far_stock_the_pocket_clears` red.\n\n## How tested\nAll of these pass. camcraft-app suites: pocket3d_open_side, operations, pocket3d_hsm, shared_face_bodies, keep_law, neighbour_law, coarse_laws, center_cut_multiaxis, setup_align, whole_model_pocket, level_links, area_controls, drill_prior, probe_op, project_roundtrip, remachining, rest_across_setups, ribbon, suppressed_rest, stock_engine_agreement, plus the lib `open_side` unit test. `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings` is clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n- The ignored heavy lanes: pocket3d_hsm's pinned move counts and stock_engine_agreement. Their whole-model 3D Pocket fixtures may cut more stock now.\n- The batch tier and the ui suites.\n- A fixture or clamp standing in the newly cleared stock. The verify fixture law judges it, but no test builds one.\n\nChangelog: A whole-model 3D Pocket (and Multi-Axis Rough) clears the stock around the model out to the stock's outline instead of stopping about two tool radii past the silhouette.\n\nEffort: high (not escalated)\nFork synced at v0.19.0\n\nFixes #1774\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
